It appears there's a slight naming convention issue. The 'CDI' (Common Rail Direct Injection) designation was used for older generations of Mercedes-Benz diesel engines. The most recent generation of the Mercedes-Benz B-Class (W247, launched 2019) uses the designation 'd' for its diesel models. The direct equivalent to a 'B180 CDI' in the current lineup would be the 'B180d'.

Since there is no "most recent version" specifically named 'B180 CDI' within the current W247 generation, and I must evaluate the exact model requested without making substitutions or assumptions, I have to return default `0.00` values due to the ambiguity.

